<title>USA: PSE&amp;G natgas competition pilot cleared.</title>
<headline>PSE&amp;G natgas competition pilot cleared.</headline>
<dateline>NEWARK, N.J. 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public Service Electric and Gas Co said Wednesday the New Jersey Board of Public Utilities has approved the utility's natural gas competition pilot program.</p>
<p>As a result, the Public Service Enterprise Group Inc subsidiary said its residential customers in four towns will have the opportunity to choose their natural gas supplier.</p>
<p>Under the program, residential customers in Piscataway, Bloomfield, Pennsuaken and Westampton can choose to purchase natural gas from a supplier other than PSE&amp;G beginning May 1.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
